About our client
Hong Kong and Asia well-established Listed Group, business involve property development, retail and supply chain, they are seeking a team leader to drive the digital transformation and enhance business processes with innovative AI solutions. 




Responsibilities & Accountabilities

Provide the overall technology vision, supporting process redesign initiatives aligned with Group’s digital transformation strategy, including AI adoption;

Serve as a strategic business partner, collaborating with senior executives and key stakeholders to identify business process improvement, validate requirements, and drive AI adoption across teams/Business Units;

Research, evaluate, and champion innovative technologies and initiatives, including chatbots, knowledge management solutions, AI Agent, agentic processes and system integration;

Collaborate closely with IT infrastructure and security teams to define technical requirements and develop solution architectures, where applicable;

Lead the design and governance of system architecture blueprint, ensuring compliance with corporate standards and industry best practices.


Qualifications & Experience 

Minimum of 10-15 years' relevant experience in business system and digital transformation, with at least 5-7 years in a leadership or management role;

Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related discipline

Solid business acumen with hands-on experience in delivering AI projects on enterprise platforms (e.g. AWS, OpenAI/ChatGPT, Microsoft, Google or related AI tools);

Proven experience in enterprise-grade systems, including ERP systems, with a strong track record in data transformation and system integration projects;

Strong negotiation, consensus-building, and stakeholder management skills with a proven ability to engage with internal customers, senior executives, and technical teams;

Excellent interpersonal skills with fluent verbal and written communication in both English and Chinese;

Strategic mindset and business acumen;

Strong leadership and influence to drive change and collaboration in complex settings.


To apply, please click on the ‘Quick Apply’ button or call Nick Chow via below website (Contact Us) for a confidential discussion.

Alternatively, email your resume (with your current and expected salary, notice period) to nick.chow@macleansgroup .com

Your interest will be treated in strict confidence and only shortlisted candidates will be notified.

www.macleansgroup.com

